ts torn  from the body of other work it is a  reassembly a patchwork quilt of meanings  already accomplished the second is the  image of the individual reader before  the universal library personally I  collect more books than I need or can  possibly even read in a single lifetime  visitors to my home sometimes as can be  really read all of these and the answer  of course is no but that isn't the point  the collector always wants to own more  that he can experience all at once it  needs to be enough to overwhelm there  must always be more possibility than  satisfaction and the collection is one  of the only ways to have too much and  not enough at the same time to be  consoled by what cannot be known  completely this is another way in which  reading a book serves some kind of  religion while immersed in a book I  always feel that that book was meant to  be read one reader at a time written  precisely for his or her particular  attention and object waiting to be lit  by a singular imagination the  interaction between reader and writer is  as intimate as a penitent and prayer if  it is well done a book will allow you to  suspend your awareness of the medium it  wants to be fed to the fires of your  attention to a demise and D materialized  like the Gnostics ol the other fantasy  of reading is the melding of multiple  consciousnesses into one giant text  exploding into levels of apprehension  enabled by radical technologies either  apprehension is lit from within by the  single and deliberate mind who  to reach another mind and that's why  books still better thank
 

